    "summary_short": "The state troopers face their most chaotic assignment yet when Farva becomes engaged to Thorny's sister, sparking an over-the-top Indian wedding celebration. Unwilling to accept Farva into his family, Thorny devises a series of outrageous schemes to break up the couple before they reach the altar. Meanwhile, a dangerous new drug ring emerges on their turf, forcing the squad to juggle undercover sabotage with actual law enforcement. To save the day, the troopers must manage to crack the case without completely destroying the wedding in the process.",
    "summary_long": "The Vermont State Troopers are back, but their newest challenge hits far closer to home than usual. Everything unravels when Farva announces his engagement to Thorny's sister, leading to a wildly extravagant Indian engagement party that quickly descends into total madness. Horrified by the prospect of Farva officially joining his family tree, Thorny immediately begins orchestrating elaborate schemes to sabotage the relationship from within. While the internal dynamic within the squad devolves into comedy and chaos, a sinister new drug operation quietly takes root in their jurisdiction, threatening local safety. Navigating a maze of absurd family dynamics, cultural missteps, and escalating rivalries, the troopers are forced to divide their energy between Thorny's petty schemes and legitimate police work. Farva's usual hot-headed antics only complicate matters, making both the investigation and the upcoming nuptials increasingly unpredictable. As the drug ring grows more pervasive, the squad must pull together their unconventional skills to crack the case before it ruins the town. Ultimately, the troopers find themselves in a high-stakes race against time where solving the crime and preserving the wedding go hand in hand. In true Super Troopers fashion, success relies on a blend of chaotic luck, unyielding brotherhood, and utter law enforcement absurdity.",
